module Stryker
  class Instrumenter
    # A mutant that got no switch, and the reason, so that a run can report
    # how many sites it skipped and why.
    #
    # The reason is one of these:
    #
    # - `:no_switch_site`: no node around the mutant's site can hold a
    #   switch. That is the case inside `BEGIN { }`, which Ruby allows only at
    #   the top level of a file. It is also the case for a class or module
    #   name, and for a statement of a kind that no row of the placement
    #   table names, such as `@count = 0` or a `for` loop, at the top level of
    #   a file or directly in a class or module body, since neither a class
    #   nor a module holds a switch.
    # - `:no_one_line_form`: the mutant's text spans several lines, and
    #   refract's formatting of it has no form on one line, as a regexp with
    #   a line break inside it. A switch on several lines would move every
    #   line after it. It is also the reason when the plain mutant parses but
    #   has no one node where the switch goes, as when `x = if c` becomes
    #   `x = if c then 5 end; if c`, so there is no text to put on one line.
    # - `:does_not_parse`: the plain mutant, the original file with only the
    #   mutant's edit made, doesn't parse, so the mutant is not valid Ruby. A
    #   run reports it with the status `CompileError` of the shared report
    #   schema.
    #
    # ## Examples
    #
    # ```ruby
    # skip = result.skipped.first
    # [skip.mutant.id, skip.reason]
    # # => [1, :no_switch_site]
    # ```
    class Skip < Data
      # Why a mutant got no switch.
      type reason = :no_switch_site | :no_one_line_form | :does_not_parse

      # The mutant that got no switch.
      attr_reader mutant: Mutant

      # Why it got none.
      attr_reader reason: reason

      # Builds the skip.
      #
      # - `mutant`: Stryker::Mutant, the mutant that got no switch.
      # - `reason`: Symbol, why it got none.
      def self.new: (mutant: Mutant, reason: reason) -> instance
                  | (Mutant mutant, reason reason) -> instance
    end
  end
end
